This repository vendors and patches several third-party projects as git
submodules (opentelemetry-collector, opentelemetry-collector-contrib,
opentelemetry-go, opentelemetry-proto, telegraf) via the corresponding
`*-patch` directories. Files under those directories that are genuine
patches on top of upstream source retain their original upstream copyright
header (e.g. "Copyright The OpenTelemetry Authors") — this is correct and
should not be changed. New, ASAP-original files (including files that live
inside a `*-patch` directory tree but implement functionality with no
upstream counterpart, such as
`opentelemetry-collector-contrib-patch/processor/asapedgeprocessor`) should
use:

    // Copyright ProjectASAP Authors
    // SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

as their header instead of copying an existing upstream-licensed file's
header.
